        {
          "beat_type": "establishing / escalation",
          "description": "The exposed catwalk in wind and darkness raises the physical stakes; the town below is mostly dark, visually confirming the scale of the crisis.",
          "approximate_location": "opening",
          "confidence": 0.93
        },
        {
          "beat_type": "tonal contradiction",
          "description": "Noah's nostalgic complaint ('I miss boring weather') and Aria's correction ('You miss boring jobs') use casual, almost wistful banter while the characters are physically endangered on a rusted catwalk in a storm — the mundane register of the dialogue sits in deliberate tension with the hazardous setting.",
          "approximate_location": "early-middle",
          "confidence": 0.88
        },
        {
          "beat_type": "discovery / turning point",
          "description": "The receiver picks up an unknown voice from Red Creek station reporting that the north shelter needs insulin and dry blankets — the first confirmation that the broadcast network is reaching people with urgent needs.",
          "approximate_location": "middle",
          "confidence": 0.97
        },
        {
          "beat_type": "emotional peak",
          "description": "Aria and Noah freeze upon hearing the distress call, marking a shift from technical problem-solving to human stakes. Aria's smile — noted as the first of the night — signals emotional release.",
          "approximate_location": "late",
          "confidence": 0.92
        },
        {
          "beat_type": "resolution beat",
          "description": "June confirms radio contact ('Loud enough to make me useful'), and Aria tightens the last bolt — the antenna mission is complete and the network is live.",
